+# Human-Readable Package Layout
+
+The package is organized around two product workflows plus small shared support modules.
+
+## `ai_ready_db_Renaissance/`
+
+User-facing local-first workflow: `local/` owns ASE workspace and exports, `cloud/` owns cloud querying/sync/upload policy, `fine_tune_planer/` owns planning and user decisions, `skills/` owns skill entry points, `evaluator/` owns coverage/cost scoring, and the Renaissance root keeps metadata, VASP adapters, and DFT finalization.
+
+## `ai_ready_db_Reforging/`
+
+Offline cloud reforging workflow: dataset ingestion, OMAT streaming, normalization, hierarchical classification, screening/routing, VASP recalculation preparation/parsing, dflow/Bohrium submission helpers, validation, deduplication, and PostgreSQL insertion.
+
+## Shared support
+
+- `core/`: shared record model, normalization, hashing, stress helpers, tags, classification, routing, and ASE conversion.
+- `chemistry/`: compact element and DFT+U detection helpers reused by `core`.
+- `database/`, `datasets/`, and `utils/`: focused infrastructure that still serves one or both workflows.
+
+New workflow-facing code should enter through `ai_ready_db_Renaissance` or `ai_ready_db_Reforging`.
