+# Ai-ready_db_Renaissance
+
+`Ai-ready_db_Renaissance` is the user-facing workflow. It initializes a local ASE SQLite database, writes VASP inputs through pymatgen adapters, finalizes completed DFT outputs into the local database, and reports the fine-tuning data gap before any new DFT calculation is scheduled.
+
+Minimal flow:
+
+```python
+from ai_ready_db.ai_ready_db_Renaissance.skills import ai_ready_db_Renaissance_start, ai_ready_db_finetune_plan
+
+ai_ready_db_Renaissance_start("renaissance_config.yaml")
+report = ai_ready_db_finetune_plan("renaissance_config.yaml")
+```
+
+The local ASE database is the private user-side data source. Structured training exports are batched into HDF5 files rather than one-sample-per-file outputs.
+
+Module layout:
+
+- `local/`: local ASE workspace, local query/export, and dataset manifests.
+- `cloud/`: PostgreSQL querying, sync, and upload policy.
+- `fine_tune_planer/`: target profiles, gap planning, user decisions, and fine-tune plans.
+- `skills/`: user-facing skill entry points, `agent_handle.py`, and the Fine Tuning MLFF skill adapter.
+- `evaluator/`: coverage and DFT cost estimates used by planning.
+
+The package root intentionally keeps only cross-cutting Renaissance pieces: config, metadata normalization, VASP I/O adapters, and DFT finalization.
+
+For agent integration, use the transport-agnostic dispatcher:
+
+```python
+from ai_ready_db.ai_ready_db_Renaissance.skills import handle_agent_action
+
+response = handle_agent_action(
+    "finetune_plan",
+    "ai_ready_db/ai_ready_db_Renaissance/examples/finetune_plan.yaml",
+)
+```
+
+`agent_handle.py` is not itself an MCP server. It is the stable Python layer that an MCP server, CLI, or other agent runtime can wrap.
+
+The repository-level FastMCP wrapper lives in `ai_ready_db.mcp_server` and exposes the stable Renaissance actions through `run_ai_ready_db_Renaissance_action`.
